    "body": "## Problem\n\nOn SM90, the layout heuristic (`csrc/jit_kernels/heuristics/sm90.hpp`) adds block M candidates of 16 and 32 when `m <= 32` for `Normal`, `Batched` and `KGroupedContiguous` GEMMs. The SM90 FP8 1D2D and BF16 kernels support these small tiles, but the SM90 FP8 **1D1D** kernel (used for FP32-output / weight-gradient GEMMs and for the k-grouped GEMM) only supports `BLOCK_M` of 64 or 128:\n\n```\ndeep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d1d.cuh(61): error: static assertion failed with \"Invalid block size\"\n      static_assert(BLOCK_M % WGMMA::M == 0, \"Invalid block size\");\ndeep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d1d.cuh(264): error: static assertion failed with \"Invalid block sizes\"\n      static_assert(BLOCK_M == WGMMA::M * (BLOCK_M <= 64 ? 1 : 2), \"Invalid block sizes\");\n```\n\nFor `m <= 32` the cost model always prefers the smaller tile (e.g. it picks `block_m=32, block_n=56` for `m=27, n=5744, k=7936`), so JIT compilation fails and the call raises. This affects, on Hopper:\n\n- `fp8_gemm_nt(a, b, d, c=d)` with an FP32 `d` (the 1D1D wgrad path) whenever `m <= 32`\n- `k_grouped_fp8_gemm_nt_contiguous` whenever `m <= 32`\n\nNeither shape was covered by the tests (the wgrad shapes only use `m` from `nk_list`, all `>= 576`, and the k-grouped shapes all have `m >= 768`). Found with a randomized shape fuzzer on an H200.\n\n## Fix\n\nOnly offer the 16/32 candidates to kernels that support them (`kernel_type != Kernel1D1D`). With the fix, the heuristic picks `block_m=64` for these shapes. Shapes with `m > 32` are unaffected, since the candidate list only changes when `m <= 32`.\n\nTests (`tests/generators.py`):\n\n- Small-M weight-gradient shapes (`m in {16, 32}`, `n=4096, k=7168`, FP32 accumulate) in `enumerate_normal`. On SM90 they use the FP8 1D1D kernel and the BF16 kernel. On SM100 they should go through swap-AB.\n- A small-M k-grouped shape (`num_groups=8, m=16, n=2048`) in `enumerate_k_grouped_contiguous`, enabled on SM90 only. 8 groups keep TMA multicast disabled, so this shape does not depend on the separate k-grouped multicast fix in #415 / #429.\n\n## Testing (H200, CUDA 13.0, PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130, at the PR head)\n\n| Suite | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `tests/test_fp8_fp4.py` | pass |\n| `tests/test_bf16.py` | pass |\n| `tests/test_layout.py` | pass |\n| `tests/test_einsum.py` | pass |\n| `tests/test_legacy.py` | pass |\n| `tests/test_attention.py` | pass |\n\nNew test lines:\n\n```\n# test_fp8_fp4.py (FP8 1D1D wgrad and k-grouped)\n > Perf (m=    16, n=  4096, k=  7168, 1D1D, layout=NT, FP32, acc=1):   19.2 us |   49 TFLOPS | 1610 GB/s | 0.81x cuBLAS speedup\n > Perf (m=    32, n=  4096, k=  7168, 1D1D, layout=NT, FP32, acc=1):   17.8 us |  106 TFLOPS | 1778 GB/s | 0.90x cuBLAS speedup\n > Perf (FP8, num_groups= 8, m=   16, n= 2048, k= 1927, gran_k=128, k_alignment=128, psum=0, acc=1, FP32):    7 us |   17 TFLOPS |  952 GB/s\n# test_bf16.py\n > Perf (m=    16, n=  4096, k=  7168, layout=TN, FP32, acc=1):    32.7 us |   29 TFLOPS | 1817 GB/s | 0.76x cuBLAS\n > Perf (m=    32, n=  4096, k=  7168, layout=TN, FP32, acc=1):    26.7 us |   70 TFLOPS | 2254 GB/s | 0.93x cuBLAS\n > Perf (num_groups= 8, m=   16, n= 2048, k= 1927, align=128, psum=0, acc=1, FP32):    8 us |   16 TFLOPS | 1513 GB/s\n# test_legacy.py (k-grouped)\n > Perf (num_groups=8, m=   16, n= 2048, k= 2304, layout=TN):    9 us |   16 TFLOPS | 1146 GB/s\n```\n\nBefore the fix, the same shapes fail at JIT compile time with the static assertions quoted above.\n\nI could only test on SM90. The k-grouped shape is gated to SM90 because I could not check whether the SM100 k-grouped kernel accepts the swap-AB layout its heuristic picks for small M. It could be enabled there if it does.\n",
